      "value": "@{5fd2a1caaeaa7e4385751606|full_name}: I disagree with your last statement - money DOES equal trust. I imagine that anyone who's prepared to spend money on their account is less likely to be a troll or a crasher because those sorts of individuals are constantly risking being banned and likely wouldn't spend money on their accounts. \nAlso, VRC+ is quite expensive and doesn't provide particularly valuable features so, more than anything else, it's basically a donation. It's like becoming a patron of a creator that you like using Patreon. I think the kind of people who spend their money like this would tend to be more mature and trustworthy.\nYou mentioned that you and your friend purchased VRC+. Do you think that you guys are evidence against my above-stated views? Do you regard yourselves as unworthy of trust?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
