      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ee4be3aa4d9f33301f550e9|full_name}: I don’t think either of us are particularly trustworthy to be entirely truthful. We’ve done nothing as far as content creation, and we’ve hardly played the game with me under 80 hours and him under 30, neither of us deserve trust ranks that fast.\nSecondly, if money = trust then that certainly didn’t work well in CSGO’s world, since they made their game free, but for a price, you can purchase the trusted addition which paired you with players who also were trusted in attempts to create an environment where cheating was less frequent. Come to find out there was zero discrepancy between trusted/non-trusted lobbies.\nSomeone with a well paying job and no hours is NOT MORE TRUSTWORTHY than someone who is unemployed, can’t afford it, but spends HOURS in game and creating content.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
